  {
    "_meta": {
      "anthropic/maxResultSizeChars": 8000,
    },
    "description": "Execute TypeScript/JavaScript against the global \`ptah\` API for multi-step workflows only.

Prefer direct \`ptah_*\` tools: they are more focused and have lower overhead. Use \`ptah.help(topic)\` to discover APIs when execute_code is necessary.

\`ptah.files\` is read-only. Never use execute_code to create or edit files; use the native CLI write/edit tools instead.

Examples:
\`const info = await ptah.workspace.getInfo(); return info;\`
\`const files = await ptah.search.findFiles('**/*.ts', 20); return files;\`",
    "inputSchema": {
      "properties": {
        "code": {
          "description": "TypeScript/JavaScript code to execute. Has access to "ptah" global object with 21 namespaces. All methods are async. Code is auto-wrapped for execution - all patterns work:
• Simple: \`await ptah.workspace.getInfo()\` or \`ptah.workspace.getInfo()\`
• With variables: \`const info = await ptah.workspace.getInfo(); return info;\`
• IIFE (any style): \`(async () => { return await ptah.workspace.getInfo(); })()\`
• Direct return: \`return "hello"\`
Results are automatically extracted from Promises. No special syntax required.",
          "type": "string",
        },
        "resultLanguage": {
          "description": "Language of a returned source string (e.g. "tsx", ".py"): an over-budget result is outlined if it parses, else cut; the full text is spooled",
          "type": "string",
        },
        "timeout": {
          "default": 15000,
          "description": "Execution timeout in milliseconds (default: 15000, max: 30000)",
          "type": "number",
        },
      },
      "required": [
        "code",
      ],
      "type": "object",
    },
    "name": "execute_code",
  },
  {
