    "description": "Harness-builder tool: install an MCP server by writing its transport config to target config files (claude -> .mcp.json, vscode -> .vscode/mcp.json, cursor -> .cursor/mcp.json). Default targets ["claude","vscode"]. scope:"workspace" (the DEFAULT) needs an open folder and refuses home-folder targets (codex, copilot, antigravity); scope:"user" installs for every workspace. Find a server with ptah_harness_search_mcp_registry and check ptah_harness_list_installed_mcp first. Supply the transport config yourself; the registry entry gives the package/URL. Returns the server key, files written and per-target warnings. The server is available to a NEW agent session only.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "properties": {
        "config": {
          "description": "Transport config. stdio: {"type":"stdio","command":"npx","args":["-y","pkg"],"env":{}}. Remote: {"type":"http"|"sse","url":"https://...","headers":{}}. "env" and "headers" are string-to-STRING maps — a numeric value such as {"PORT":3000} is rejected, send {"PORT":"3000"}. "command" and "url" must be non-empty.",
          "type": "object",
