    "name": "ptah_task_check",
  },
  {
    "_meta": {
      "anthropic/maxResultSizeChars": 8000,
    },
    "annotations": {
      "destructiveHint": false,
    },
    "description": "Link the calling session (the chat session that makes this call; you never pass a session id) to a task folder under .ptah/specs. The link is stored per user, outside the repository, and does not edit task.md. role is primary or related (default primary); a new primary link demotes the existing one. The task folder is not checked: a missing task shows as missing in the UI. Errors: invalid-args, organization-unavailable (always in VS Code), unattributed-caller (the session has no SDK id yet; retry later), link-failed.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "properties": {
        "role": {
          "description": "Link role; defaults to primary.",
          "enum": [
            "primary",
            "related",
          ],
          "type": "string",
        },
        "taskId": {
          "description": "Task folder name (one path segment), e.g. TASK_2026_580_9f77",
          "type": "string",
        },
      },
      "required": [
        "taskId",
      ],
      "type": "object",
    },
    "name": "ptah_session_link_task",
  },
  {
    "_meta": {
      "anthropic/maxResultSizeChars": 8000,
    },
    "description": "Hand this session off to a new chat session. A child starts its successor in the same worktree and branch, passes on running lanes, and notifies its parent. The successor receives prompt as its first message. Write the handoff document first: handoffPath must be an existing absolute file path, and prompt must name it. Call once. The result states tabOpened (false: no window took the tab; it is in the session list). Refusals are returned as text with a code. Every ptah_session_* result ends with any completion a child produced while this session was not live ("Held while this session was not live").",
    "inputSchema": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "handoffPath": {
          "maxLength": 1000,
          "minLength": 1,
          "type": "string",
        },
        "label": {
          "maxLength": 60,
          "minLength": 1,
          "type": "string",
        },
        "prompt": {
          "maxLength": 102400,
          "minLength": 1,
          "type": "string",
        },
      },
      "required": [
        "handoffPath",
        "prompt",
      ],
      "type": "object",
    },
    "name": "ptah_session_handoff",
  },
  {
    "_meta": {
      "anthropic/maxResultSizeChars": 8000,
    },
    "description": "After reading HANDOFF.md and adopting the work, acknowledge the handoff to close the predecessor session. Retry when the result is retryable-failure. Do not retry a refused result; report its reason to the user.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "handoffPath": {
          "type": "string",
        },
        "predecessorSessionId": {
          "type": "string",
        },
      },
      "required": [
