    "description": "List exported symbols per file from the graph export index (ts,js,tsx,py,go,cs files; not the SQLite code index of ptah_code_search_symbols), one page at a time, ordered by path. Use to find where a symbol is exported from or map the exports of a directory (narrow with pathPrefix). Returns { count, total, offset, nextOffset?, files }; pass nextOffset as offset for the next page (absent on the last page). Defaults: no prefix, limit 30 (max 1000), offset 0. A page ends early at the result size limit; a file too large on its own comes alone, with truncated: true, symbolCount, and symbolsFile (a JSON file of its symbols) or symbolsFileError. On very large workspaces the graph is partial: the result then has incomplete: true with graphedFiles and discoveredFiles, and a missing file or empty list is not conclusive. While the graph builds in the background (minutes on a large workspace) the result is { status: "building", retryAfterMs }: call again after retryAfterMs.",
